# Milestone: M5
# Covers: determinism rule D-cross-1 — chained event dispatch; 4 events where
#         each subscriber emits the next event in the chain; verify subscriber
#         ordering is byte-stable across 100x3 preset runs.
#
# blocked: cross-spec event chain gap + string concat (T46 dropped) blocks expected output
# matrix-row: reactive-event
#
# Reason:
#   Requires Event.new() T59 stdlib binding and scratch-frame body dispatch.
#   The chain ordering (e0 fires → sub emits e1 → sub emits e2 → sub emits e3)
#   depends on urbi_event_emit_async queuing behaviour: each emit enqueues
#   subscriber bodies on the deferred event ring (spec #3 §6.1), which drains
#   in FIFO registration order.  The chain correctness is exercised by
#   test_event_emit_async.c at the C level.
#
#   When active: byte-identical output across 100 runs under each of the 3
#   tunable presets (default, footprint, URBI_GC_NONE) per D-cross-1.
#   Total chain log: 4 events × 50 dispatches = 200 deterministic lines.
#
# Activate at T59 by replacing the source below with the uncommented version.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var e0 = Event.new();
#   var e1 = Event.new();
#   var e2 = Event.new();
#   var e3 = Event.new();
#   var seq = "";
#   at (e0?) { Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "0"; e1! };
#   at (e1?) { Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "1"; e2! };
#   at (e2?) { Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "2"; e3! };
#   at (e3?) Realm.seq = Realm.seq + "3";
#   var i = 0;
#   while (i < 50) { e0!; Realm.i = i + 1 };
#   seq
#   --- expected output (50 repetitions of "0123") ---
#   [00000001] "01230123...0123"
